      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Plans, limits, and billing</h2>
      <h3>Free plan</h3>
      <p>
        The Free plan includes access to all 18 tools with no watermark on output. Free limits
        include:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Up to 50 MB per file</li>
        <li>Up to 5 PDFs per merge batch</li>
        <li>3 PDF → Word or Excel exports per calendar day</li>
        <li>Unlimited use of client-side organize and convert tools (merge, split, compare, OCR,
          sign, and others that run in your browser)</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Pro plan</h3>
      <p>
        PDFTwin Pro costs <strong>$9 USD per month</strong> and includes everything in Free, plus:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Up to 200 MB per file</li>
        <li>Unlimited PDF → Word and Excel exports</li>
        <li>Unlimited merge batch size (6 or more PDFs in one merge)</li>
        <li>Priority server processing when available</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Pro subscriptions are billed monthly through PayPal until you cancel. Payment details are
        collected and processed by PayPal — Helios Impex does not receive or store your card number or
        bank credentials. By subscribing, you authorize recurring monthly charges at the price
        shown at checkout.
      </p>

      <h3>Cancellation and refunds</h3>
      <p>
        You may cancel Pro at any time through your PayPal account (Settings → Payments → Manage
        automatic payments). Cancellation stops future billing; Pro access continues until the end
        of the current paid period. Refunds are handled under PayPal&rsquo;s policies. There is no
        separate free trial — the Free plan lets you evaluate all tools at no cost before upgrading.
      </p>

      <h3>Plan enforcement</h3>
      <p>
        We enforce Free-plan limits through file-size checks, server-side daily export counters,
        and client-side merge batch gates. Attempting to bypass these limits or misrepresent your
        plan status is a violation of these Terms.
      </p>
    </section>

