    <section>
      <h2>Output quality and tool limitations</h2>
      <p>
        PDFTwin is provided as a productivity tool, not a certified legal, financial, or compliance
        service. You should review all outputs before relying on them.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Document conversion</strong> — PDF → Word/Excel and Word → PDF quality depends on
          source layout complexity. Scanned PDFs may need OCR before conversion; complex designs
          may require manual cleanup.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>OCR</strong> — Optical character recognition runs locally in your browser and may
          contain errors, especially on low-quality scans or handwriting.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Compare PDF</strong> — Side-by-side viewing helps review differences but is not
          a substitute for legal redlining or certified document comparison.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Sign PDF</strong> — Adds a visual signature image (drawn or uploaded). It is not
          a qualified electronic signature under eIDAS, ESIGN, or similar regulations unless your
          jurisdiction and use case explicitly allow image signatures.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Lock &amp; unlock</strong> — Unlocking works for restriction-only PDFs and empty
          passwords. Encrypted files require the correct password; we cannot recover lost passwords.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
